In article <113kdfINNav5@agate.berkeley.edu> datta@durban.berkeley.edu (Ruchira Datta) writes:
>I am playing on my 386SX under DOS version 3.30.  I have Nethack Version 3.0j;
>I downloaded the binaries directly from linc.cis.upenn.edu.  I have
>encountered a particular problem several times, although this is the first
>time it has caused a crash.  Under certain circumstances, when I hit ^P (to
>repeat the last message), I get:
>
>Write fault error writing device PRN
>Abort, Retry, Ignore, Fail?
>
>(I think the circumstances are, that the screen was being redrawn when I hit
>^P, for example after an inventory was done.  I suppose I play too fast.)

OK, DOS interrupts all keyboard requests to check for special codes.
^P instructs dos to echo all con output to prn and con. This continues until
reset (I don't remember the code). To avoid the problem, the dev team has
a flag to put in nethack.cnf (I think it is rawio) that will instruct dos
not to scan for IOCTRL (similiar to binary transfers). The ansi driver
has no problem with this either since it sees binary codes anyway.
Hope this helps.

